window.FIELD_CHAPTER_PARTS["book-3-full-book"] = window.FIELD_CHAPTER_PARTS["book-3-full-book"] || {};
window.FIELD_CHAPTER_PARTS["book-3-full-book"][66] = "<h1>Appendix B. Practice data and SQL scripts [as of 2026-10]</h1>\n<p><strong>What this is.</strong> The SQL in C13.6a, in the worked examples and exercises of C13, and in the practice plan of C37 runs on small invented datasets. This appendix gives the three short scripts that build them and the queries the chapters quote, so you can run every one and see the numbers the chapters report. All data are invented; none describes a real product or user.</p>\n<p><strong>How to run.</strong> Save each script in a file with the name in its first line and run it with Python 3, which includes SQLite and needs nothing else. Date and string functions differ between databases, so check your own dialect before copying a query to another system. Each script prints its results; the numbers quoted in the chapters were checked against them.</p>\n<p><strong>Which chapter uses which script.</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Script</th>\n<th>Dataset</th>\n<th>Used in</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>5,000 users and their events over three weeks, with three acquisition channels (seed 42)</td>\n<td>C13.6a and its worked examples and exercises; the analytics practice in C37</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Three weekly cohorts of 2,000 signups whose channel mix shifts while each channel's rate stays fixed (seed 11)</td>\n<td>C13.6a, the mix-shift example</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>A &quot;test table&quot; of 10,000 visits, 2,400 add-to-carts and 600 purchases, with 300 repeat add-to-carts</td>\n<td>The funnel-count exercise in C13</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span id=\"app-b-b-1-script-1-the-practice-dataset-and-its-queries\"></span>\n<h2>B.1 Script 1: the practice dataset and its queries</h2>\n<p>Key results to expect: the funnel returns 5,000 signed up, 2,574 activated and 530 purchased; activation by channel is 53.7% (organic, 2,248 signups), 40.1% (paid, 1,745) and 66.2% (referral, 1,007); the fan-out query returns 7,574 rows for 5,000 users; the two definitions of week-1 return give 107 and 745.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\"># Script 1: the practice dataset (5,000 invented users) and the queries run on it in C13 and C37.\n# Run: python3 practice_data.py   (creates sandbox.db in the current folder; needs only Python, which includes SQLite).\nimport sqlite3, random, datetime as dt\nrandom.seed(42)\ncon=sqlite3.connect('sandbox.db'); c=con.cursor()\nc.executescript(&quot;&quot;&quot;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS users; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS events;\nCREATE TABLE users(user_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, signup_date TEXT, channel TEXT);\nCREATE TABLE events(user_id INTEGER, event TEXT, event_date TEXT);\n&quot;&quot;&quot;)\nstart=dt.date(2027,1,4)  # a Monday\nchannels=[('organic',.45,.55,.30),('paid',.35,.40,.20),('referral',.20,.65,.35)]  # name, share, p_activate, p_week1_return|activated\nuid=0\nfor i in range(5000):\n    uid+=1\n    d=start+dt.timedelta(days=random.randint(0,20))\n    r=random.random(); acc=0\n    for name,sh,pa,pr in channels:\n        acc+=sh\n        if r&lt;=acc: ch=name; pact=pa; pret=pr; break\n    c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO users VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;,(uid,d.isoformat(),ch))\n    c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;,(uid,'signup',d.isoformat()))\n    if random.random()&lt;pact:\n        ad=d+dt.timedelta(days=random.randint(0,2))\n        c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;,(uid,'activated',ad.isoformat()))\n        if random.random()&lt;pret:\n            rd=d+dt.timedelta(days=random.randint(7,13))\n            c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;,(uid,'returned',rd.isoformat()))\n        if random.random()&lt;0.22:\n            pd=d+dt.timedelta(days=random.randint(1,10))\n            c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;,(uid,'purchased',pd.isoformat()))\ncon.commit()\n\nQUERIES = [\n    (&quot;C13.6a, a funnel in one pass&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='signup'    THEN user_id END) AS signed_up,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='activated' THEN user_id END) AS activated,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='purchased' THEN user_id END) AS purchased\nFROM events;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;C13.6a, a rate by segment&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT u.channel,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id) AS signups,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT a.user_id) AS activated,\n       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT a.user_id) / COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id), 1) AS activation_pct\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN events a ON a.user_id = u.user_id AND a.event = 'activated'\nGROUP BY u.channel;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;C13.6a, a cohort by signup week&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT strftime('%Y-%W', u.signup_date) AS signup_week,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id) AS signups,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT r.user_id) AS returned,\n       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT r.user_id) / COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id), 1) AS return_pct\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN events r ON r.user_id = u.user_id AND r.event = 'returned'\nGROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;C13 worked query, daily active users (first six days shown)&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT event_date, COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) AS active_users\nFROM events\nWHERE event IN ('signup', 'activated')   -- whichever events define &quot;active&quot;\nGROUP BY event_date\nORDER BY event_date;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;C13 worked query, two definitions of week-1 return (107 and 745)&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN CAST(julianday(r.event_date) - julianday(u.signup_date) AS INT) BETWEEN 1 AND 7\n                           THEN u.user_id END) AS returned_days_1_to_7,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN CAST(julianday(r.event_date) - julianday(u.signup_date) AS INT) BETWEEN 7 AND 13\n                           THEN u.user_id END) AS returned_days_7_to_13\nFROM users u\nJOIN events r ON r.user_id = u.user_id AND r.event = 'returned';\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;C13 worked query, return rate by channel and signup week&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nWITH base AS (\n  SELECT u.user_id,\n         strftime('%Y-%W', u.signup_date) AS signup_week,\n         u.channel,\n         MAX(CASE WHEN e.event = 'returned'\n                   AND CAST(julianday(e.event_date) - julianday(u.signup_date) AS INT) BETWEEN 7 AND 13\n                  THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS returned\n  FROM users u\n  LEFT JOIN events e ON e.user_id = u.user_id\n  GROUP BY u.user_id)\nSELECT signup_week, channel, COUNT(*) AS signups, SUM(returned) AS returned,\n       ROUND(100.0 * SUM(returned) / COUNT(*), 1) AS return_pct\nFROM base GROUP BY signup_week, channel ORDER BY signup_week, channel;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;Failure: fan-out (7,574 rows for 5,000 users)&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT COUNT(*)\nFROM users u JOIN events e ON e.user_id = u.user_id AND e.event IN ('signup', 'activated');\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n    (&quot;Failure: an inner join removes the denominator (1,208 of 1,208 for organic)&quot;, &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT u.channel, COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id)\nFROM users u JOIN events a ON a.user_id = u.user_id AND a.event = 'activated'\nGROUP BY u.channel;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;),\n]\nfor title, q in QUERIES:\n    print('\\n##', title)\n    for i, row in enumerate(c.execute(q)):\n        if i == 6: print('...'); break\n        print(row)\n</code></pre>\n<span id=\"app-b-b-2-script-2-a-mix-shift\"></span>\n<h2>B.2 Script 2: a mix shift</h2>\n<p>Key results to expect: overall activation falls from 53.95% to 51.10% to 47.50% by signup week, while each channel's own rate stays about the same; the decomposition from week 1 to week 3 gives a rate effect of −1.41 points and a mix effect of −5.04 points, a total of −6.45 points.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\"># Script 2: a synthetic dataset for C13.6a in which overall activation falls week over week while every channel's rate stays the same (seed 11).\n# Run: python3 mixshift.py\nimport sqlite3, random, datetime as dt\nrandom.seed(11)\ncon = sqlite3.connect(&quot;:memory:&quot;); c = con.cursor()\nc.executescript(&quot;CREATE TABLE users(user_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, signup_date TEXT, channel TEXT, activated INTEGER);&quot;)\nrate = {&quot;organic&quot;: .54, &quot;paid&quot;: .40, &quot;referral&quot;: .66}\nmix = {1: [(&quot;organic&quot;, .50), (&quot;paid&quot;, .20), (&quot;referral&quot;, .30)],\n       2: [(&quot;organic&quot;, .45), (&quot;paid&quot;, .35), (&quot;referral&quot;, .20)],\n       3: [(&quot;organic&quot;, .35), (&quot;paid&quot;, .50), (&quot;referral&quot;, .15)]}\nstart = dt.date(2027, 3, 1); uid = 0\nfor w in (1, 2, 3):\n    for _ in range(2000):\n        uid += 1; r = random.random(); acc = 0\n        for ch, sh in mix[w]:\n            acc += sh\n            if r &lt;= acc: break\n        d = start + dt.timedelta(days=7 * (w - 1) + random.randint(0, 6))\n        c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO users VALUES(?,?,?,?)&quot;, (uid, d.isoformat(), ch, 1 if random.random() &lt; rate[ch] else 0))\ndef run(title, q):\n    print(&quot;\\n##&quot;, title)\n    for r in c.execute(q): print(r)\nbase = &quot;CAST((julianday(signup_date)-julianday('2027-03-01'))/7 AS INT)+1&quot;\nrun(&quot;Q1 overall activation by signup week&quot;, f&quot;&quot;&quot;SELECT {base} AS wk, COUNT(*) AS signups, SUM(activated) AS activated,\n ROUND(100.0*SUM(activated)/COUNT(*),2) AS activation_pct FROM users GROUP BY wk ORDER BY wk&quot;&quot;&quot;)\nrun(&quot;Q2 by week and channel: share of signups and activation rate&quot;, f&quot;&quot;&quot;WITH t AS (SELECT {base} AS wk, channel, COUNT(*) AS n, SUM(activated) AS a FROM users GROUP BY wk, channel),\n w AS (SELECT wk, SUM(n) AS total FROM t GROUP BY wk)\nSELECT t.wk, t.channel, t.n, ROUND(100.0*t.n/w.total,1) AS share_pct, ROUND(100.0*t.a/t.n,1) AS rate_pct\nFROM t JOIN w USING(wk) ORDER BY t.wk, t.channel&quot;&quot;&quot;)\nrun(&quot;Q3 decomposition week 1 to week 3 (rate effect at old shares, mix effect at new rates, percentage points)&quot;, f&quot;&quot;&quot;WITH t AS (SELECT {base} AS wk, channel, COUNT(*) AS n, SUM(activated) AS a FROM users GROUP BY wk, channel),\n w AS (SELECT wk, SUM(n) AS total FROM t GROUP BY wk),\n s AS (SELECT t.wk, t.channel, 1.0*t.n/w.total AS share, 1.0*t.a/t.n AS rate FROM t JOIN w USING(wk)),\n x AS (SELECT s1.channel, s1.share AS sh1, s1.rate AS r1, s3.share AS sh3, s3.rate AS r3 FROM s s1 JOIN s s3 ON s1.channel=s3.channel AND s1.wk=1 AND s3.wk=3)\nSELECT ROUND(100*SUM(sh1*(r3-r1)),2) AS rate_effect_pp, ROUND(100*SUM((sh3-sh1)*r3),2) AS mix_effect_pp,\n ROUND(100*SUM(sh3*r3)-100*SUM(sh1*r1),2) AS total_change_pp FROM x&quot;&quot;&quot;)\nrun(&quot;Q4 mix-adjusted activation at the week-1 mix&quot;, f&quot;&quot;&quot;WITH t AS (SELECT {base} AS wk, channel, COUNT(*) AS n, SUM(activated) AS a FROM users GROUP BY wk, channel),\n w AS (SELECT wk, SUM(n) AS total FROM t GROUP BY wk),\n s AS (SELECT t.wk, t.channel, 1.0*t.n/w.total AS share, 1.0*t.a/t.n AS rate FROM t JOIN w USING(wk))\nSELECT ROUND(100*SUM(s1.share*s3.rate),2) AS week3_rates_at_week1_mix FROM s s1 JOIN s s3 ON s1.channel=s3.channel AND s1.wk=1 AND s3.wk=3&quot;&quot;&quot;)\n</code></pre>\n<span id=\"app-b-b-3-script-3-the-funnel-count-exercise\"></span>\n<h2>B.3 Script 3: the funnel-count exercise</h2>\n<p>Key results to expect: 10,000 users visited, 2,400 added to cart and 600 purchased; counting <code>add_to_cart</code> rows instead of users gives 2,700.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\"># Script 3: the &quot;test table&quot; of the exercise on funnel counts in C13 (invented): 10,000 users visited, 2,400 added to cart,\n# 600 purchased, and 300 of the users who added to cart did so on two different days.\n# Run: python3 test_table.py\nimport sqlite3\ncon = sqlite3.connect(&quot;:memory:&quot;); c = con.cursor()\nc.execute(&quot;CREATE TABLE events(user_id INTEGER, event TEXT, event_date TEXT)&quot;)\nfor u in range(1, 10001): c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;, (u, &quot;visit&quot;, &quot;2027-02-01&quot;))\nfor u in range(1, 2401): c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;, (u, &quot;add_to_cart&quot;, &quot;2027-02-01&quot;))\nfor u in range(1, 301): c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;, (u, &quot;add_to_cart&quot;, &quot;2027-02-02&quot;))\nfor u in range(1, 601): c.execute(&quot;INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?)&quot;, (u, &quot;purchase&quot;, &quot;2027-02-02&quot;))\nprint(&quot;users per step:&quot;, c.execute(&quot;&quot;&quot;SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='visit' THEN user_id END),\n       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='add_to_cart' THEN user_id END),\n       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN event='purchase' THEN user_id END) FROM events&quot;&quot;&quot;).fetchone())\nprint(&quot;add_to_cart rows (the wrong count):&quot;, c.execute(&quot;SELECT COUNT(*) FROM events WHERE event='add_to_cart'&quot;).fetchone()[0])\n</code></pre>\n<span id=\"appendix-c\"></span>\n";
